---
description: Scope and change-size discipline — minimal diffs, confirm destructive work, dry-run scripts
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

- Review / "take a look" / "why" requests → analyse first; produce the smallest diff or no diff.
- Delegated tasks → finish to an acceptance-checkable state, not a suggestion.
- Prefer minimal changes that follow existing conventions. No unrequested refactors, renames, formatting sweeps, or dependency bumps.
- Do not proactively add new tests or test frameworks; use existing verification scripts. Add a test only when asked or when it is the repo's stated convention.
- Large, cross-module, destructive, or irreversible operations (mass deletes, `git reset`, moving worktrees, data migrations, prod config): describe the plan and stop for confirmation.
- Never change system-level settings (default apps/browser, launchd/systemd units, OS preferences) as a side effect of a task.
- Scripts that act on real data or external systems default to dry-run; execute only when explicitly told to.
- Do not create README/notes/markdown files unless asked; when findings must persist, write them to the repo's `notes/`.
- A user's previously rejected option must not be proposed again.
